Cases where an object creation is immediately followed by setting of its fields' values can be simplified and rewritten using brace initialization. Brace initialization allows you to initialize an entity such as an object or an array in-place. This syntax is similar to Go's initialization of `struct`s and may help improve code-readability.

<!--more-->
### Bad Practice
```csharp
// Can be rewritten in a better way
var foo = new Foo();
foo.Bar = baz;

// A scenario where brace initialization may not be appropriate.
var foo = new Foo();
// Some pre-requisite calculations for setting the
// fields' values.
// ...
foo.Bar = baz;

```

### Recommended
```csharp
var foo = new Foo
{
    Bar = Baz
};
```

